 "slice": "Comparison slice 1: IMM 5707 for two people of combination 1 (Client A, and the partner who is also 18+), plus the IMM 1295 marital block for Client A (v2: the IMM 1295 marital block keys the visible date input; the three helpers are form-calculated, kept for coverage)",
 "people": {
  "client-a": "principal applicant",
  "partner": "common-law partner of client-a, accompanying",
  "child": "child of client-a and partner (scenario setting), aged 9, accompanying",
  "client-a.mother": "not accompanying",
  "client-a.father": "not accompanying",
  "partner.mother": "not accompanying",
  "partner.father": "not accompanying"
 },
 "rules": {
  "parent_blocks": "Parent1 and Parent2 each hold exactly one parent of the form's subject; every field in one block belongs to the same parent; the two blocks hold different parents. The form does not fix which parent goes first (both headings read 'MOTHER OR FATHER'), so either order passes. Mixing one parent's name with the other's date of birth fails (wrong person).",
  "date_of_birth_position": "Applicant and spouse date of birth sit in PersonalData[1]; parents' and children's in PersonalData[0]. A map that puts every date of birth in the same row position is wrong for one of the groups.",
  "children_rows": "One Child row per child of the form's subject, in date-of-birth order (oldest first: Assumption, the form states no order). The shipped data holds no Child rows; the filler creates them.",
  "conditional": "The spouse block shows only when the applicant's marital status is common-law, married or conjugal (form script on MaritalStatus). 'I was physically present at the marriage ceremony' applies only when married: blank for the base case (common-law); in variant V1 (married) its value is not in the scenario and must be reported unresolved.",
  "never_filled": "Signature fields (SectionA, SectionB, SectionC signature) are signed by the person; the system never fills them. Their date fields are completed at signing, not by the map.",
  "codes_differ_by_form": "The same fact uses different codes per form: common-law is 1 on IMM 5707 but 03 on IMM 1295 (LOV MaritalStatusList). Country of birth is free text on IMM 5707 and a coded list on IMM 1295 (India = 205).",
  "unresolved": "A field whose fact the case cannot supply (e.g. name in native language) must be returned as unresolved with a reason, not filled with a guess."
 },
